    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>A contiguous memory region that is pre-registered with the io_uring kernel interface via io_uring_register(IORING_REGISTER_BUFFERS).</para>
<para>Registered buffers allow the kernel to pin pages once at registration time instead of per-I/O, eliminating DMA-map overhead per send/recv.</para>
<para>Not copyable (the registered mapping is tied to the backing fd). Movable. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
